From: Au-Zone Technologies <support@au-zone.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: nxp: dwc-mipi-csi2: Enable device tree links

The receiver records the sensor as its source when the sensor binds, but the
link was created disabled and cannot be enabled afterwards because the source
is already set. The pipeline then fails to start with EPIPE. Create the link
enabled and immutable, as a device tree link to a single source should be.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Ezurio patch 0057 is not upstream]

---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/nxp/dwc-mipi-csi2.c b/drivers/media/platform/nxp/dwc-mipi-csi2.c
index b8c770753747..131e7bcfdf55 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/nxp/dwc-mipi-csi2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/nxp/dwc-mipi-csi2.c
@@ -1322,7 +1322,9 @@ static int dwc_csi_notify_bound(struct v4l2_async_notifier *notifier,
 	struct dwc_csi_device *csidev = notifier_to_dwc_csi_device(notifier);
 	struct media_pad *sink = &csidev->sd.entity.pads[DWC_CSI2RX_PAD_SINK];
 
-	int ret = v4l2_create_fwnode_links_to_pad(sd, sink, 0);
+	int ret = v4l2_create_fwnode_links_to_pad(sd, sink,
+						  MEDIA_LNK_FL_ENABLED |
+						  MEDIA_LNK_FL_IMMUTABLE);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(csidev->dev, "Couldn't link pad for subdev %s, ret: %d\n",
 			sd->name, ret);
